       "content": "```python\ndef comb_sort(arr):\n    n = len(arr)\n    if n <= 1:\n        return arr\n    \n    gap = n\n    swapped = True\n    \n    while gap > 1 or swapped:\n        gap = max(1, int(gap / 1.3))\n        swapped = False\n        \n        for i in range(n - gap):\n            if arr[i] > arr[i + gap]:\n                arr[i], arr[i + gap] = arr[i + gap], arr[i]\n                swapped = True\n    \n    return arr\n```",
       "name": null,
       "reasoning": "The user wants me to implement a comb sort algorithm in Python. Comb sort is an improvement over bubble sort. It works by comparing elements separated by a gap, which shrinks by a factor of 1.3 (or 10/13) in each iteration until the gap becomes 1, at which point it becomes a bubble sort.\n\nLet me implement this:\n\n1. Calculate initial gap as length of list / 1.3\n2. While gap > 1 or swapped is True:\n   - Update gap = gap / 1.3 (rounded down to integer)\n   - If gap < 1, set gap = 1\n   - Compare elements separated by gap and swap if needed\n   - Track if any swaps occurred\n\nLet me write the code.",
